notes: Classic GAP README still teaches a sequential 15-step live chain. AEP 2.8.5 live path is seal a capsule, freeze the clock at seal, wait 1000 ms then run every check together then Apply. The fifteen named rows are a derived ledger, not a second live pass. Skip is not used. Closed-wall Deny names the closed walls. Layer 1 constrained decoding stays an authoring gate, not Admit. Layer 3 must name Base Node kernel pulse plus collect-all Admit. Authoring a .gap file is not the check. Who-may is agent_may, not trust_ring ranks. Fit analysis is docs/CLASSIC-GAP-VS-AEP-2.8.5.md on thePM001/GAP. Ticket close is coding close.
acceptance: Classic GAP README no longer teaches a sequential 15-step live combinator. Layer 3 names freeze-at-seal, 1000 ms kernel pulse, collect-all Admit then Apply. Fifteen named rows are a derived ledger. Skip is not a live verb. Who-may is agent_may. Constrained decoding is named as authoring, not Admit. nla-policy-scan gate writing-mode-rules on the rewritten README.
bac: nla-policy-scan gate writing-mode-rules
